  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through Sunday) \nIssued at 1233 PM CDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nUpper heights will rise over the region Monday night into Tuesday\nand will peak Tuesday night into Wednesday (at 500mb). Headline-\nworthy heat and dry weather can be expected. There is some hint of\nan eastward extension of the low-level thermal ridge across\nnorthern OK Wednesday afternoon ahead of a front over KS, so that\ncould add a few degrees to an already hot forecast across NE OK.\n\nNow to the good news. The ridge will break down quickly as an\nupper trough develops over the Great Lakes and Northeast. Both the\nGFS and EC develop a band of showers and storms along the KS front,\ndropping south into the region Wednesday night into Thursday. The\nmodel blend PoPs (NBM) have increased to likely across the north,\ndefinitely a good sign when you are in a drought. The outflow- \nreinforced boundary is expected to make a good southward push into\nthe area Thursday, knocking temps back a bit. In fact, the new \nforecast for Thursday and Friday has highs below 100 areawide.\nTemps are likely to rebound over the weekend as the boundary\nretreats back north ahead of what could be a stronger system and\ncold front the following week. There are at least signs in the\nmodels that fall is coming. Stay tuned.\n\nLacy",
